  "tested_head": "da3e2b157a5e0d9dfb98dafe2fe9646159719a4f",
  "title": "Bound repeated Go build information diagnostics (R3.12)",
  "body": "## Problem\n\nEvery aligned, pointer-encoded Go build information candidate with an unreadable version pointer appends the same owned diagnostic string. A damaged region can therefore retain hundreds of thousands of identical strings while the reader continues looking for valid metadata. The whole-file fallback can probe the same offsets again.\n\n## Change\n\nCount these failed probes locally and emit one diagnostic after each candidate scan. A single failure keeps its exact existing text; repeated failures retain the specific reason and count. The count explicitly describes probes in that scan, rather than unique file offsets.\n\nThe scan still reaches later readable inline or pointer-encoded build information. Module diagnostics, address mapping, function decoding, input limits and the public API remain unchanged. There is no new dependency.\n\nThe public R3.12 claim is commit `ace2048a1d6e9424bf5aa31e399119cabdb63659`, before implementation. ROADMAP and STATUS record the completed work and evidence.\n\n## Regression and native evidence\n\n- Six permanent integration tests cover ordinary metadata, exact single-failure wording, repeated failures before valid inline metadata, fallback rescanning without valid metadata, 32/64-bit pointer metadata in both byte orders, and invalid-width/unaligned controls. Against original `3ce1ce9f`, two controls pass and four bounded-diagnostic cases fail; the fixed implementation passes all six.\n- Go 1.24.13 compiles an original owned program. Native `debug/buildinfo.ReadFile` agrees on the original and relocated complete controls; `go tool nm` verifies the original `main.main` and `main.retained` addresses in each generated image.\n- The stress image places 262,144 unreadable pointer headers in an 8 MiB region before the byte-identical native build information block. Both reader versions recover identical complete metadata and all 1,786 decoded functions. Every report field other than the intentionally aggregated top-level diagnostic is compared directly, with matching full-report hashes.\n- Ordinary control reports, including diagnostics, remain identical. The native Go reader is used for the complete controls; it is not claimed to accept a damaged prefix or to execute the transformed images.\n\n## Measured retention\n\nActual public `go::inspect` calls run in fresh processes under identical optimized Rust 1.99.0 builds, with only `go.rs` swapped between original and fixed code. Release LTO is disabled, codegen-units is 16 and debug information is disabled in both builds.\n\n| 8 MiB repeated-header fixture | Original peak RSS, KiB | Fixed peak RSS, KiB |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Process 1 | 47,620 | 14,160 |\n| Process 2 | 47,504 | 14,224 |\n| Process 3 | 47,504 | 14,124 |\n| Median | 47,504 | 14,160 |\n\nMedian peak RSS falls **70.2% on this bounded fixture**. There are twelve measured processes in total, including the original, relocated and single-failure controls for both builds. This is repeated-diagnostic aggregation, not a reduced scan limit or omitted metadata.\n\n## Validation\n\n[Full validation at `da3e2b1`](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43069839827/job/130694422683):\n\n- Complete formats suite: **1,711 passed, 0 failed, 10 ignored** across 208 test targets.\n- Rust 1.99.0 formatting, strict all-target formats Clippy, layers, locks and secrets passed.\n- The complete five-crate WebAssembly gate passed.\n- Original/fixed comparisons, native controls, fresh-process measurements and a clean checkout passed.\n\n[Final source identity and documentation checks](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43071242390) verify that final `8779ef0` changes only ROADMAP and STATUS relative to the fully tested implementation, retaining the entire product/test/dependency tree and the claim-before-code ancestry.\n\nTwo earlier validation runs stopped while constructing the native ELF fixture, before any product tests: [first attempt](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43068899521), [second attempt](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43069518509). The corrected fixture relocates the whole program-header table instead of treating zero section-header bytes as free space. Those failures remain recorded.\n",
